id: pm-r8yytk
title: Shape-qualified scale baselines drifted from current CLI/SDK output contracts and supported runtime
description: "The committed scratch 10k scale budget still uses the legacy unqualified tier key and July output/startup observations. Exact-main and feature-branch runs now deterministically emit richer list/get payloads and exceed Node 24/26 cold mutation ceilings while all measured outputs remain below the 5k product target. Refreshing the baseline requires explicit cross-head evidence, the existing 25 percent methodology, and preservation of product ceilings."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[5]: "area:cli","area:performance","area:sdk",benchmark,regression
created_at: "2026-09-01T14:41:40.376Z"
updated_at: "2026-09-01T17:16:45.507Z"
closed_at: "2026-09-01T17:16:44.964Z"
completed_at: "2026-09-01T17:16:44.964Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: The scratch 10k budget is shape-qualified; exact-main and delivery-head results are compared on the supported Node 24 workflow baseline; a five-iteration delivery-head run establishes measured budgets with 25 percent headroom; the unmodified scale check passes; every command remains below the published 1000 ms p95 and 5000-token product targets; Node 26 variance is recorded without being misreported as a delivery regression.
parent: pm-9rxu
risk: high
confidence: high
severity: high
resolution: Normalized both scale tiers to shape-qualified keys while retaining measured regression headroom and the independent hard product-target gate.
expected_result: Scale manifests are shape-unambiguous and every actual command remains constrained by p95 and token product targets.
actual_result: "Fresh Node 24 scratch:10,000 CLI and SDK benchmark passed 3 iterations with p95 <= 1,000ms and actual tokens <= 5,000."
component: performance
